{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/428559-gift-of-the-elementals-question","id":428559,"title":"Gift of the Elementals Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-04T20:58:14-08:00","id":428559,"title":"Gift of the Elementals Question","content":"Howdy.<br /> <br /> I just bought 2e, and I'm liking it so far. I like the idea of creating an Ithaeur and unleashing a can of elemental whoop-ass. However, I'm not sure how using influence with elements would work in combat. What kind of damage do they do? What are the special effects? How do enemies resist getting a big rock thrown at them? That sort of thing. I can't seem to find a good way of answering the question. Anything y'all know that I seem to be missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3183-shomaxt","name":"Shomaxt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T21:18:05-08:00","id":428611,"title":"","content":"<b>Do not mess with elder werewolves!</b><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://cdn.collider.com/wp-content/uploads/pompeii-volcano.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T21:19:18-08:00","id":428614,"title":"","content":"What Incendax is trying to say is that given enough of the proper renown, enough experience, and the right level of creative genius a werewolf can essentially bring up a volcano in the middle of Times Square if he so chose and that's on the extreme end of the powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T21:23:36-08:00","id":428643,"title":"","content":"I'm not talking about the extreme end of things though. What happens when I use a lighter and manipulate flames to send out a stream of fire? How do others defend against it? What does it do to them and their health boxes?<br /> <br /> I ask this because I know that this sort of thing is going to come up with my group, and without any sort of guide on that end my storyteller is going to have a hard time coming up with a suitable answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3183-shomaxt","name":"Shomaxt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T02:01:39-08:00","id":428871,"title":"","content":"Purity 4 = firebending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T02:29:24-08:00","id":428887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shomaxt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/428559-gift-of-the-elementals-question?p=428643#post428643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not talking about the extreme end of things though. What happens when I use a lighter and manipulate flames to send out a stream of fire? How do others defend against it? What does it do to them and their health boxes?<br /> <br /> I ask this because I know that this sort of thing is going to come up with my group, and without any sort of guide on that end my storyteller is going to have a hard time coming up with a suitable answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Make a simple roll as if you were using either a gun or a throwing weapon (your choice, but it depends on how you go about targeting the stream of fire) wich involves a Dexterity + Athletics (throwing) or Firearms (as if a gun). Damage is determined by the fire source as usual, even one success deals the full damage. Isn't a Fire Damage chart somewhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T02:57:30-08:00","id":428899,"title":"","content":"There's one in the Vampire book. I think the only difference between damage for vamps/prometheans and everything else is the type inflicted so it should work fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T03:05:22-08:00","id":428904,"title":"","content":"Oh, so no chart in Werewolf? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I thought that would be part of the &quot;general rules&quot; part of the book. It is stand-alone isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T03:14:51-08:00","id":428927,"title":"","content":"The Gift of the Elementals is a challenging one because it's comparatively freeform next to a lot of other supernatural powers that are available. Exactly how you might attack someone with Influence (Fire), for example, depends on your level of mastery of it and the context. Someone already on fire? Use Strengthen to increase the damage they're taking. Want to lash someone with flame from a torch or whatnot? Use the Control dice pool as an attack pool, with damage dealt based on the flame intensity as normal. No fire around? Just snap your fingers and Create fire, using the same style of attack but no need for a source.<br /> <br /> Of course I don't have my comp copy yet so not sure whether the fire rules ended up in the core <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll probably write up a broader sample of uses for the Gift of the Elementals in a bit, to help illustrate how to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T10:13:45-08:00","id":428940,"title":"","content":"Set self on fire. Shift to Gauru. Kick vampire ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T10:20:04-08:00","id":428945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/428559-gift-of-the-elementals-question?p=428940#post428940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Set self on fire. Shift to Gauru. Kick vampire ass.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as the vampire isn't wearing an obfuscated set of silver spiked armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T10:37:17-08:00","id":428967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/428559-gift-of-the-elementals-question?p=428940#post428940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Set self on fire. Shift to Gauru. Kick vampire ass.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we have an <i>Izidakh</i> infiltrator here!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T08:46:24-07:00","id":437078,"title":"","content":"This thread seems to need a bump as it has some good questions that don't seem like they've been answered yet.<br /> The original question was what is this good for at the low end. A starting character would have, at most, two dots in anything, which would mean Strengthening one of the elements for tens of minutes or Manipulating it for a few minutes. Being as you only get two Shadow Gifts to start (and it seems like they're supposed to be two different onces, not two facets of the same one), it seems like the Cataclysm option is at least an unlikely starting option. What would any of these look like, though?<br /> <br /> That's to Chris for pointing out a good use for Strengthen (Fire). Something that's on fire is takes more damage. Any thoughts on where the line is between Manipulating (Fire) and Controlling (Fire)?<br /> <br /> What about the other elements? Being as the Auspice and Tribe with Elementals as a starting gift both have Wisdom as their primary Renown, Influence (Water) would be a common-ish choice. What does it mean to Strengthen water? Or air for that matter, if you had an Irakka Bone Shadow or an Ithaeur Iron Master?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T08:56:48-07:00","id":437084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/428559-gift-of-the-elementals-question?p=428940#post428940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Set self on fire. Shift to Gauru. Kick vampire ass.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're on fire, then the vampires can't grapple you! Why didn't I think of this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T09:06:38-07:00","id":437095,"title":"","content":"Remember that Strengthen can change the Resonant condition to Open. At low levels, it might be a clever way to summon allies (though of course, Spirits aren't guaranteed to help you just 'cause you opened the door for them). If your totem is a compatible type you could theoretically use Influence on yourself or your packmates to make them Open, which could allow the totem to Manifest through you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T09:22:27-07:00","id":437105,"title":"","content":"That's a good point. So someone with Heart of Water and 2 dots of Wisdom could find a puddle and, for half an hour or so, turn it into a semi-open door for spirits to Reach through and do as they see fit? Is it then only Open to spirits of the Water umia, or can anything Reach through if something is Open?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T09:28:19-07:00","id":437109,"title":"","content":"You technically wouldn't need a puddle. All packmates have the resonant condition to their totem. So if your totem is resonant with water, you're resonant with water. You may actually be able to use this with Strengthen [any element], incidentally, providing you have the right totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T09:40:54-07:00","id":437126,"title":"","content":"I guess the point of clarification I'm looking for at the moment is that, for these Facets to be useful in this way, would you need a totem that's also an elemental?<br /> My plan (and most of the totems I've seen mentioned in the fiction anthology or the core book) was to have a conceptual spirit as a totem. (Restraint is one used in the anthology. Pain is mentioned in a rite write-up. I was planning on Unity). Would this usage only allow spirits of the element provided by the gifts? I mean, it is called Gift of the Elementals, so it would make sense that Elementals benefit from giving it out...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T09:55:36-07:00","id":437142,"title":"","content":"That's only if you want to use the facet to bring spirits over. As it is you can strengthen the conditions of the element. Water can take better advantage of water banes, water could be more effective at losing scent if you're being hunted, it could be harder to fight against if you're trying to drown someone, like in the fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T10:46:26-07:00","id":437219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/428559-gift-of-the-elementals-question?p=437142#post437142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it is you can strengthen the conditions of the element. Water can take better advantage of water banes, water could be more effective at losing scent if you're being hunted, it could be harder to fight against if you're trying to drown someone, like in the fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are good examples. Thanks. By &quot;like in the fiction&quot; do you mean the story where the Bone Shadow is doing the rite where he gets burried?<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any other thoughts on Strengthening Water or Air?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T10:54:39-07:00","id":437232,"title":"","content":"In the Werewolf the Forsaken Second Edition book there's a continuing tale told before each new chapter where a pack of Uratha is dealing with beshilu. It shows very well the dangers of the hunt even against minor enemies if a werewolf doesn't think ahead and the prey gets lucky. It also shows the dedication some Forsaken show to their task, as the pack ends up on a hunt for two years.<br /> <br /> Strengthening air might work to clear an area of gasses, or help with CPR. It might be able to keep you afloat if you were relying on the wind to do something. It couldn't steer you in a certain direction, that would probably be Manipulate or Control. In addition to helping disperse a scent you could probably use it to let a scent linger longer than it might normally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T17:00:57-07:00","id":437720,"title":"","content":"Here's some ideas beyond fire, in addition to the universal spirit-related uses. Mass create I didn't bother with since, you know, it's just more of create or more permanent creation.<br /> <br /> Water:<br /> Strengthen: Provide a penalty to someone swimming as the water 'thickens' and becomes hard to move through. Make it so water you have 'lasts longer' before you need to check for deprivation. Make it so a smaller amount of water can be used to douse a fire. Enhance the strength of existing waves or movement of water to a larger degree. Purify drinkable water.<br /> Manipulate: Provide a much bigger penalty to swimming, perhaps making it contested as the water more actively moves against someone. Cause rain nearby to fall 'around' something to keep it dry. Dry something off that's wet by displacing the water. Stop up a sink or other minor water source. Enhance the strength of existing waves or movement of water to a larger degree.<br /> Control: Change water vapor to liquid, liquid to ice, or visa versa (could be used to short circuit something on a humid day, easily). Attempt to actively drown someone by forcing water into their lungs (whether they're swimming or you just have another source onhand) which would likely be akin to a grapple. Drag someone through water when they're swimming. Actively part a rainstorm around a small area, keeping the area dry. Keep a boat from sinking, or stop up some other high pressure water source. Cause a violent wave in a lake or ocean.<br /> Create: All sorts of things can be done with this, as you're creating water from nowhere. You can likely drown someone without an existing water source, or cause no small amount of damage by using water to create short circuits or get people electrocuted inside a powered building.<br /> <br /> Air:<br /> Strengthen: Breathe in thin air with no penalty. Hold your breath longer (I'd add a minute/turn per success). Cause the wind to blow faster (maybe adding or subtracting dice to whatever bonus/penalty, like archery or flying a plane). Thicken fog to make perception penalties even worse. Lighten a fog by strengthening the 'clear' air in the area. Purify air to make it more breathable.<br /> Manipulate: Create a light wind (great for scattering papers and causing minor chaos indoors). Do CPR without touching someone. Change the direction the wind is blowing. Create an area of 'thin' air, likely causing some penalties to chases or other in depth athletics. Clear fog away entirely (the fog oriented things probably also fall under water, btw).<br /> Control: Create a much stronger gust, likely capable of knocking people down or causing huge problems to flying creatures/vehicles. Create a small cyclone. Cause the air to follow you, forming a bubble underwater or in other similar conditions. Cause a vacuum to suffocate someone, snuff fires out, and similar. Perform acts akin to clumsy telekinesis using much more concentrated movements of air. Breathe without needing to expand or contract your lungs (likely worth some stealth bonuses, help you appear dead).<br /> Create: Again, all sorts of things. Create air in a vacuum or when already underwater. Do more finesse-oriented telekinesis, maybe even fly, depending on your ST. Create more dangerous cyclones or other bits of locally oriented weather.<br /> <br /> Earth (I'm assuming Metal is its own influence if not in raw ore form):<br /> Strengthen: Bonuses to stone weaponry and similar, more damage with thrown rocks or the like. Harden the ground, dirt, stone, or natural barriers, making it hard to break them. Make quicksand less dangerous. More easily cut diamonds (by hardening a diamond based tool). Intensify an earthquake locally. Make a gemstone appear to be worth more.<br /> Manipulate: Trip people up on land by making it shift and move a bit. Remove your own penalties to move across rough terrain. Shape stonework more easily. Create miniature landslides, or large ones where it's already fairly hazardous and loose. Bend/warp tools made with natural stone or the like. Walk safely across quicksand or across mud without getting stuck. Cause a minor tremor.<br /> Control: Turn stones from one kind to another (easy Resources from turning rocks to diamonds comes to mind). Shape a stone (perfectly 'cut' diamonds, for instance) completely with no other effort. Cause a foundation to shift enough to collapse a building. Create small earthquakes. Create weapons from raw materials in an instant. Create a larger landslide from nothing. Trap people by making the earth or stone jut out and grab them, or form around them. Create little 'natural grenades' by making rocks explode upon impact.<br /> Create: Again, a lot, but a few examples that come to mind. Bury someone alive out of nowhere. Fill a room, trapping everyone inside. Create a much more noticeable earthquake (locally). Create gemstones and other valuables, or natural weapons out of nowhere.<br /> <br /> <br /> And of course, when you use the facet that expands the radius of these, your options grow even more.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T10:55:53-08:00","id":808041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/428559-gift-of-the-elementals-question?p=428927#post428927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gift of the Elementals is a challenging one because it's comparatively freeform next to a lot of other supernatural powers that are available. Exactly how you might attack someone with Influence (Fire), for example, depends on your level of mastery of it and the context. Someone already on fire? Use Strengthen to increase the damage they're taking. Want to lash someone with flame from a torch or whatnot? Use the Control dice pool as an attack pool, with damage dealt based on the flame intensity as normal. No fire around? Just snap your fingers and Create fire, using the same style of attack but no need for a source.<br /> <br /> Of course I don't have my comp copy yet so not sure whether the fire rules ended up in the core <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll probably write up a broader sample of uses for the Gift of the Elementals in a bit, to help illustrate how to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been reading all the discussions on the forum about the Gift of the Elementals, and I think we are in dire need to more official examples of what the boundaries are. Please! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}